<item>
            <title>[ZEPPELIN-5] Tutorial notebook fails if fs.defaultFS is set to non-local FS in Hadoop core-site.xml</title>
                <link>https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/ZEPPELIN-5</link>
                <project id="12316221" key="ZEPPELIN">Zeppelin</project>
                    <description>&lt;p&gt;I&apos;ve noticed that if fs.defaultFS is set to a non-local FS (like HDFS) in the Hadoop core-site.xml, the Zeppelin Tutorial notebook will fail to find the example data because it will attempt to look in, for example, hdfs://master-node:hdfs-port/data/bank-full.csv instead of looking in the local filesystem, where the tutorial downloaded the data files just a few lines earlier.  This can be fixed by prepending the url with &quot;file://&quot; in the call to sc.textFile().&lt;/p&gt;</description>
                <environment></environment>
        <key id="12785593">ZEPPELIN-5</key>
            <summary>Tutorial notebook fails if fs.defaultFS is set to non-local FS in Hadoop core-site.xml</summary>
